# The Broker card: the connection this client holds on a radio's behalf.
#
# It is the one card on the Status screen that reports on something the *radio* cannot see. A
# radio with `proxy_to_client_enabled` hands over a message and is told nothing about what
# happened to it - the firmware's publishQueuedMessages() runs every 200 ms whether or not a
# broker is reachable - so from the radio, and from every other screen on this client, a proxy
# that is failing looks exactly like one that is working.
#
# Four situations, in the order they are worth telling apart. Only the first is the one people
# expect; the other three are the reason the card exists.

scene demo
delay 300
config

tab radio
stats
hold 900

# Working. Green heading, a server the radio never named - an empty MQTTConfig.address means the
# public broker, and that substitution happens here rather than on the radio, so the Settings
# screen shows a blank Server field while this says where the traffic is actually going.
broker connected
hold 2200

# Connected, and for the ninth time. Every single frame of a flapping link says "Connected"; the
# sign-in count is the only thing on the screen that disagrees, and the reason it last dropped
# stays up after it comes back.
broker flapping
hold 2400

# Refused. The card goes red, the retry is on its own backoff, and the sentence names the host
# and the reason - which is a whole line and so a note rather than a value.
broker refused
hold 2400

# And the fault with no error behind it. Connected, publishing, subscribed to nothing, because
# every channel on this radio has downlink turned off. Nothing logs it and nothing fails; as far
# as MQTT is concerned everything worked. The Topics row is the only place it is visible.
broker silent
hold 2600

# And the client's own refusal, which is the one state the radio cannot be blamed for. The
# connection rows are gone rather than showing zeros - "none subscribed" here would put a warning
# on the radio's channels for something the Brick decided - and what is left is the count of
# messages the radio offered with nowhere to put them.
broker disabled
hold 2600
